      "text": "Step 6: Apply the product-to-sum identities or known product formulas for sines. For simplicity, use the identity for the product of sines of angles in arithmetic progression:\n\\[\n\\sin x \\sin (60^\\circ - x) \\sin (60^\\circ + x) = \\frac{1}{4} \\sin 3x\n\\]\nFor $x = 20^\\circ$, we have:\n\\[\n\\sin 20^\\circ \\sin 40^\\circ \\sin 80^\\circ = \\frac{1}{4} \\sin 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\n\\]",
